    finding: 'In two hourly diary studies, 35% (Study 1) and 43% (Study 2) of behaviors were habits, done almost daily and usually in the same place. During habits, people’s thoughts matched what they were doing only 40% and 44% of the time, compared with 70% and 60% during non-habitual behavior.',
